{"message_id":"c4eb3444-f9f1-4bad-8e5a-6827ff52cf73","timestamp":"2026-05-13T06:15:21.312521Z","version":"1.0","source_id":"jarvis","event_type":"result","project":null,"correlation_id":"670a5386-fca7-4785-b8e6-c138f20c2fda","payload":{"command":"chat","result":{"response":"Session ended. \n\nQuick recap of what you covered:\n- **Dagger soliloquy** — hallucination as pre-murder guilt, supernatural imagery, measured questioning\n- **Banquo's ghost** — public breakdown, fragmented imperatives, loss of control\n- **Comparative analysis** — tracking Macbeth's psychological decline across two key hallucination scenes\n- **Grade 9 techniques** — structural awareness, language detail, Jacobean context, AO4 comparison\n\nYou were operating at a strong level throughout — particularly in your comparative analysis and attention to language choices. If you want to pick this up again, we could move on to Lady Macbeth's sleepwalking scene, the blood imagery arc across the play, or practice structuring a full exam answer on these themes.","tools_called":[],"correlation_id":"670a5386-fca7-4785-b8e6-c138f20c2fda"},"correlation_id":"670a5386-fca7-4785-b8e6-c138f20c2fda","success":true}}
